A||N||3||Eric_PA||VSS Question (electrical specs?)||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||12-05-2001||09:36 PM||||I'm wondering if anyone is familiar with the VSS signal after it is conditioned from the guages. In particular, is it 2000 ppm or 4000 ppm? Also what are the voltage levels, constant or increase with speed. <P>The reason for this is because I am planning on making a circuit to convert this signal to a square wave to be accepted by the new ecm. So if there are any sites or available technical information on this, please help me.<P>Thanks,<BR>Eric||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eric_PA||12-06-2001||06:43 AM||||Anyone....<BR>I have conflicting information on the VSS signal from the dash. Is it 2000 PPM or 4000 PPM. Also, what kind of output does the optical vss put out? I need to somehow get a signal to the ecm so it works corectly with a manual tied to it. (90 3800 conversion using the 8253 ECM) I tried using the stock Fiero VSS for this swap, but it doesn't send a good signal to the ECM.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000002||William Federle||12-06-2001||08:24 AM||||The signal from the transmission-mounted unit<BR>is 4000 pulses/mile. On the board behind the speedometer it is converted to 2000 pulses per mile for the electronics other than the speedometer.<P>I tried to use the 2000 pulse/mile signal for my digital speedometer and it didn't work. I had to use the 4000 pulse per mile signal. I don't think the 2000/mile one was strong enough. <P>I always thought the 2000/mile signal was already a square-wave (0v to 5v). I guess I don't know for sure but since it's generated on the board I'll bet it is.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||12-06-2001||08:47 AM||||Eric,<P>  I was building a calibration station for air-coil guages and played some with the Fiero speedo.  The original Fiero VSS from my '87 auto puts out a sine wave - to + that varies in freq and amplitude.  Although I'm not familiar with the ECM you're playing with, I would think that the signal needs to be conditioned which means halved (or not) for freq, but definitely needs chopped into a square wave and probably stregthened to be a consistent voltage.  The Fiero speedo does exactly that 2K/mi square wave 0 to + and  I don't recall the voltage. I'll need to dig out my notes for that.||||reg||1
